  "scope": "Official implementation research and read-only GPU profiling of two existing diagnostic inputs per model; no dependency, model weights, runtime or user-setting changes.",
  "conclusions": [
    "The current Qwen baseline does not exercise its fused convolution/GatedDeltaNet kernels. Correcting this execution path is necessary before treating earlier branch-cache timings as representative of an optimized Qwen engine.",
    "Replace per-path tensor snapshots with native sequence/state handles and batched frontier advancement. MiniCPM5-2B standard Llama is the simpler first native-backend target.",
    "A backend must expose full-vocabulary-normalized, pre-grammar probabilities. Native grammar/sampling logprobs can describe a different distribution and silently change beam ranking.",
    "Profiler counts support investigating kernel/host-call fragmentation and state ownership. They do not measure the speedup of an unimplemented kernel/backend."
  ],
